  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "🐉 Chinese Dragon Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Names for Chinese dragons, made from real Chinese words, with their meanings."
    },
    "intro": "The Chinese dragon, or long, is a wise, lucky creature of water and weather, not a fire-breathing monster: it brings rain, rules rivers and seas, and guards pearls. This **Chinese dragon name generator** makes names from real Chinese words, like Leiyun for thunder cloud, with their meanings and a title.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "The Chinese dragon",
        "content": "<p>The Chinese dragon, the <em>long</em>, is a creature of water and weather, not fire: it brings rain, rules rivers and seas, and stands for luck and power.</p><ul><li><strong>The Dragon Kings</strong> of the Four Seas ruled the waters in Chinese folk religion, and people prayed to them for rain.</li><li><strong>The emperor's dragon:</strong> under the Ming and Qing dynasties, the five-clawed dragon was reserved for the emperor.</li><li><strong>The zodiac:</strong> the Dragon is one of the twelve animals of the Chinese zodiac; recent Dragon years were 2012 and 2024, and the next is 2036.</li><li><strong>Dragon boats</strong> race at the Duanwu festival, in early summer.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Naming a Chinese dragon",
        "content": "<p>Every name joins two real Chinese words, written in pinyin without tone marks, and shown with their meaning.</p><ul><li><strong>Weather and water:</strong> Leiyun (thundercloud), Heilei (black thunder), Xinghai (sea of stars).</li><li><strong>Seasons and light:</strong> Xuechun (spring snow), Chunshui (spring water).</li><li><strong>Add a title</strong> for its domain, like Lord of the Rain Clouds.</li><li><strong>Canon dragons,</strong> like the Azure Dragon Qinglong and Shenlong, are left out, as are real place names.</li></ul><p>For the Western, fire-breathing kind, try the <a href=\"dragon-name-generator.html\">Dragon Name Generator</a>.</p><p>For more gods and legends, see all the <a href=\"../categories/mythology-names.html\">mythology name generators</a>.</p><p>Writing a wuxia or xianxia story? See the <a href=\"../categories/wuxia-names.html\">wuxia and xianxia name generators</a> for heroes, sects and techniques.</p>"
      }
    ],
